To solve this problem, we can model it as a graph problem where we want to find the maximum number of disjoint cycles in the graph. Each cycle represents a group of people who can donate kidneys to each other.

Here is the Minizinc code to solve this problem:

```minizinc
include "globals.mzn";

% Input data
int: num_people = 8;
array[1..num_people] of set of int: compatible = [
  {2, 3},
  {1, 6},
  {1, 4, 7},
  {2},
  {2},
  {5},
  {8},
  {3}
];

% Variables
array[1..num_people, 1..num_people] of var bool: transplants;

% Constraints
constraint forall(i in 1..num_people) (
  sum(j in 1..num_people) (transplants[i, j]) <= 1
);
constraint forall(j in 1..num_people) (
  sum(i in 1..num_people) (transplants[i, j]) <= 1
);
constraint forall(i in 1..num_people, j in 1..num_people) (
  transplants[i, j] -> j in compatible[i]
);
constraint forall(i in 1..num_people) (
  sum(j in 1..num_people) (transplants[i, j]) = sum(j in 1..num_people) (transplants[j, i])
);

% Objective
solve maximize sum(i in 1..num_people, j in 1..num_people) (transplants[i, j]);

% Output
output [
  "{",
  "\"transplants\": [",
  join(",\n", [
    "[" ++ join(", ", [if transplants[i, j] then "1" else "0" | j in 1..num_people]) ++ "]"
    | i in 1..num_people
  ]),
  "]",
  "}"
