% Start time of each task
array[int, int] of var int: start_time;

% Makespan
var int: makespan;

% Objective: minimize makespan
solve minimize makespan;

% Constraints
constraint forall(j in 0..num_jobs-1) (
    forall(t in 1..num_tasks[j]-1) (
        start_time[j, t] >= start_time[j, t-1] + task_data[j, t-1].2
    )
);

constraint forall(m in machines) (
    cumulative(start_time, task_data, makespan)
);

% Calculate makespan
constraint makespan >= max(j in 0..num_jobs-1, t in 0..num_tasks[j]-1) (
    start_time[j, t] + task_data[j, t].2
);

output [
    "{",
    "\"makespan\": ", show(makespan),
    "}"
];
```

This model uses the `cumulative` global constraint to ensure that a machine can only work on one task at a time. The `start_time` array represents the start time of each task, and the `makespan` variable represents the total time taken to complete all jobs. The objective is to minimize the `makespan`. The constraints ensure that no task for a job can be started until the previous task for that job is completed, and that a task, once started, must run to completion.

