constraint a - b >= 2; % since a - b is a prime number
constraint a * b = n * n;
constraint is_prime(a - b);

predicate is_prime(int: x) =
  x > 1 /\ forall(i in 2..ceil(sqrt(x))) (x mod i != 0);

constraint p = a - b;

solve satisfy;

output [
    "{",
    join(",", [
        "\"" ++ "a" ++ "\": " ++ show(a),
        "\"" ++ "b" ++ "\": " ++ show(b),
        "\"" ++ "n" ++ "\": " ++ show(n),
        "\"" ++ "p" ++ "\": " ++ show(p)
    ]),
    "}"
];
```

This model uses the `is_prime` predicate to check if `a - b` is a prime number. The `solve satisfy` statement finds the smallest value of `a` that satisfies all the constraints. The `output` statement prints the values of `a`, `b`, `n`, and `p` in JSON format. 

